===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[agent noun|Agent noun]] of [[abolish]]; one who abolishes. {{defdate|From the 16<sup>th</sup> century.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1548|translator=w:Nicholas Udall|title=The First Tome or Volume of the {{w|Paraphrases of Erasmus|Paraphrase of Erasmus}} vpon the Newe Testamente|location=London|publisher=Edward Whitchurche|section=Luke 16|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A16036.0001.001
|passage={{...}} I am not come to bee an '''abolisher''' of the lawe.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1725|author=w:Henry Bourne|title=Antiquitates Vulgares: or, The Antiquities of the Common People|location=Newcastle|section=Preface, p. x|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004875177.0001.000
|passage=I would not be thought a Reviver of old Rites and Ceremonies to the Burdening of the People, nor an '''Abolisher''' of innocent Customs, which are their Pleasures and Recreations {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author={{w|Kingsley Amis}}|chapter=After Goliath|title=A Look Round the Estate: Poems 1957-1967|location=New York|publisher=Harcourt, Brace & World|pages=7-8|url=https://archive.org/details/lookroundestate00amis
|passage=Alastors, Austenites, A-test<br>'''Abolishers'''—even the straightest<br>Of issues looks pretty oblique<br>When a movement turns into a clique,}}

